cuments/s44907/appendix-6-2026-27-allocated-budget-bridges.pdf","committee":"Infrastructure Services Committee","date":"18/06/2026","key":false}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Clinical and Adult Social Work Governance Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Aberdeenshire Council","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-29","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-26","committee":"Aberdeenshire Council","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-09","committee":"IJB Audit Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-10","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-06-24","committee":"Clinical and Adult Social Work Governance Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-06-25","committee":"Aberdeenshire Council","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-02","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"10.15 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-11","committee":"IJB Audit Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"The Council expects to require external borrowing by year-end as internal resources deplete, during a period when interest rates are expected to remain elevated","lead":"Understanding when councils must refinance and what rate environment they'll face is critical for assessing future financing costs and financial sustainability","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Treasury Management Update","paper_url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47547/47547.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Three LOBO loans totalling \u00a330.5m were called with proposed rates 2-3 percentage points higher than existing rates; Council chose to repay at par","lead":"A lender needs to track when councils face material refinancing events and how those are managed; this shows Aberdeenshire had a substantial short-term funding requirement and sufficient liquidity to execute the optimal decision","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Treasury Management Update","paper_url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47547/47547.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Repayment of three market loans requires ongoing monitoring of future refinancing needs","lead":"Lender needs visibility of council's refinancing schedule and what rates they will face when loans mature; temporary internal borrowing is not a long-term solution","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"Business Services Financial Performance Update","paper_url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47543/47543.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Business Services Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Treasury Management Update","paper_url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47547/47547.pdf","headline":"The Council expects to require external borrowing by year-end as internal resources deplete, during a period when interest rates are expected to remain elevated","detail":"The Council has undertaken no new long-term external borrowing in the current year, choosing to manage cash balances using internal resources instead. This approach is temporary: the paper states that replacement borrowing will be required as internal resources reduce. This refinancing need will arise in a market environment where 'market expectations have shifted away from further near-term rate reductions towards a more prolonged period of higher rates.'","category":"borrowing","matters":"Understanding when councils must refinance and what rate environment they'll face is critical for assessing future financing costs and financial sustainability","figures":"No new long-term borrowing in financial year to date; Investment income \u00a3522K to end June 2026","quote":"As internal resources reduce later in the year, replacement borrowing may be required through either temporary borrowing or long-term borrowing, depending on market conditions, liquidity requirements and the Council's approved strategy.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Business Services Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Treasury Management Update","paper_url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47547/47547.pdf","headline":"Three LOBO loans totalling \u00a330.5m were called with proposed rates 2-3 percentage points higher than existing rates; Council chose to repay at par","detail":"DCL Paris loans of \u00a310.0m and \u00a35.5m, and an FMSWM loan of \u00a315.0m, were called with proposed new rates of 6.70%, 6.72%, and 7.48% respectively, compared to existing rates of 3.70%, 4.40%, and 4.65%. The Council exercised its repayment option to avoid accepting these higher rates. The decision avoided further obligation to the higher rates and created no breakage costs, but generates a \u00a330.5m refinancing requirement.","category":"borrowing","matters":"A lender needs to track when councils face material refinancing events and how those are managed; this shows Aberdeenshire had a substantial short-term funding requirement and sufficient liquidity to execute the optimal decision","figures":"\u00a310.0m at 3.70% (proposed 6.70%); \u00a35.5m at 4.40% (proposed 6.72%); \u00a315.0m at 4.65% (proposed 7.48%); total \u00a330.5m","quote":"The lender option exercises resulted in proposed revised rates that were significantly above the existing loan rates. The Council therefore exercised its option to repay the loans without breakage cost.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Business Services Committee","paper_title":"Business Services Financial Performance Update","paper_url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47543/47543.pdf","headline":"Repayment of three market loans requires ongoing monitoring of future refinancing needs","detail":"Council has repaid three market loans ahead of maturity, avoiding exposure to higher revised rates. However, this creates a refinancing event and future borrowing requirement that must be monitored in the uncertain interest rate environment. Treasury notes no new long-term borrowing undertaken yet, relying instead on temporary internal borrowing.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Lender needs visibility of council's refinancing schedule and what rates they will face when loans mature; temporary internal borrowing is not a long-term solution","figures":"3 market loans repaid; no new long-term borrowing undertaken","quote":"The repayment of three market loans avoided exposure to significantly higher revised rates, although this will require ongoing monitoring of future refinancing requirements.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Business Services Committee","paper_title":"Business Services Financial Performance Update","paper_url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47543/47543.pdf","headline":"Council emphasises reserves are finite; cannot provide recurring funding for structural deficit","detail":"While current drawdowns are limited and within reserve purpose, council explicitly states reserves cannot solve structural challenges: \"Reliance on reserves do not remove the need to identify and deliver recurring savings and sustainable budget solutions.\" This signals reserves are a depleting asset.","category":"reserves","matters":"Confirms council cannot rely on reserves to bridge structural gap; future depends on delivering recurring savings or service contraction","figures":"(specific reserve balances not provided in main report)","quote":"Reserves are a finite resource and can only provide temporary support. The Council continues to face significant medium-term financial challenges and reliance on reserves do not remove the need to identify and deliver recurring savings and sustainable budget solutions.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Business Services Committee","paper_title":"Business Services Financial Performance Update","paper_url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47543/47543.pdf","headline":"Two high-rated tactical budget risks (residual score 12) identified but not detailed in main report","detail":"The Directorate Risk Register contains two tactical risks with residual score of 12, flagged as requiring continued strategic visibility and active management. The document warns that materialisation \"could impact on the overall financial position,\" but specifics are contained in Appendix 2 and not detailed in the main report.","category":"governance","matters":"Known material risks indicate expected pressures; lender needs visibility of what they are and recovery plans if they crystallise","figures":"2 tactical risks, residual score 12","quote":"There are currently 2 tactical risks with an updated residual score of 12 indicating the need for continued strategic visibility and these are being actively managed by the Directorate Management Team. Should these risks materialise, this could impact on the overall financial position.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Aberdeenshire","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"The Council expects to require external borrowing by year-end as internal resources deplete, during a period when interest rates are expected to remain elevated","lead":"Understanding when councils must refinance and what rate environment they'll face is critical for assessing future financing costs and financial sustainability","also":["34 other findings in this window","6 papers caught"],"watch":"Clinical and Adult Social Work Governance Committee on 2026-09-23","n_findings":35,"n_documents":6,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 4 - Treasury Management Update","top_paper_url":"https://aberdeenshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s47547/47547.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":143,"news_drafts_total":3}}